1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,720
 Have you ever placed a trade because a chatbot said so?

2
00:00:02,720 --> 00:00:05,280
 Asking a chatbot what to buy feels smart.

3
00:00:05,280 --> 00:00:07,440
 Why? Because it's read the whole internet.

4
00:00:07,440 --> 00:00:10,000
 But think about the guy who's read every newspaper.

5
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:11,360
 He sounds smart too.

6
00:00:11,360 --> 00:00:13,440
 He has an opinion on every stock.

7
00:00:13,440 --> 00:00:15,440
 But has he tested on any of it?

8
00:00:15,440 --> 00:00:17,520
 No, that's a chatbot.

9
00:00:17,520 --> 00:00:20,160
 Well, read isn't the same as tested.

10
00:00:20,160 --> 00:00:22,880
 When you ask it what to buy, you get an opinion.

11
00:00:22,880 --> 00:00:26,320
 It sounds right, but nobody has actually checked whether it was correct.

12
00:00:26,320 --> 00:00:30,240
 So someone did, with real money, and the results are shocking.

13
00:00:30,240 --> 00:00:32,480
 In a competition called Alpha Arena,

14
00:00:32,480 --> 00:00:38,480
 six chatbots used $10,000 of real money to trade crypto for about two weeks.

15
00:00:38,480 --> 00:00:41,040
 Four of the six lost money.

16
00:00:41,040 --> 00:00:44,000
 The best one made about $2,000.

17
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:48,080
 And the worst one, GPT-5, lost about $6,000.

18
00:00:48,080 --> 00:00:50,320
 Almost half of it in just two weeks.

19
00:00:50,320 --> 00:00:54,320
 These are the same kinds of AI people ask for stock picks every day.

20
00:00:54,320 --> 00:00:56,320
 The problem isn't that AI is dumb.

21
00:00:56,320 --> 00:00:57,920
 It's that it's an opinion.

22
00:00:57,920 --> 00:01:02,160
 No matter how smart it sounds, it hasn't been tested.

23
00:01:02,160 --> 00:01:04,080
 So don't ask it what to buy.

24
00:01:04,080 --> 00:01:05,600
 Ask it to build your rules.

25
00:01:05,600 --> 00:01:09,760
 Then test those rules on past prices before you put in real money.

26
00:01:09,760 --> 00:01:12,160
 Comment cube, and I'll send you how you can do this too.

